 add(alk,25,'84','Combustion of alkanes and activity','Complete combustion of alkanes in excess oxygen produces carbon dioxide, water and heat: CH4+2O2→CO2+2H2O+heat. Limited oxygen causes incomplete combustion and produces poisonous carbon monoxide, water and unburnt carbon; the source gives 3CH4+4O2→2CO+6H2O+C. The page also gives a model-building activity for the first five alkanes and alkenes and a self-assessment.');
 add(ole,26,'85','Alkenes and the first five homologues','Hydrocarbons used as fuels are mainly carbon and hydrogen and release energy on combustion; the source gives CH4(g)+2O2(g)→2H2O(g)+CO2(g)+heat. Alkenes (olefins) are unsaturated hydrocarbons with at least one C=C double bond; general formula CnH2n. Ethene C2H4 is the simplest. The table lists ethene/ethylene C2H4 (CH2=CH2), propene/propylene C3H6 (CH2=CHCH3), butene/butylene C4H8 (CH2=CHCH2CH3), pentene C5H10 and hexene C6H12.');
 add(ole,27,'86','Alkene structural/dot-cross formulas and naming rules','The source draws structural and electron dot/cross formulae for the first five alkenes through hexene. IUPAC naming rules: choose the longest chain containing the C=C; derive the name from the matching alkane and replace −ane by −ene; number from the end nearest the double bond; assign the double bond the lowest locant, using the first double-bond carbon; and indicate branch positions with locants.');
 add(ole,28,'87','Naming alkenes and preparation by alcohol dehydration','Examples include ethene, propene, 1-butene, 2-butene, 2,3-dimethyl-2-butene and 2,3,4-trimethyl-3-hexene. Alkenes can be prepared from saturated compounds by elimination, removing atoms/groups from adjacent carbons to form a double bond. Alcohol dehydration removes water: ethanol heated with concentrated H2SO4 at 180°C forms ethene and water.');
 alk.summary.en+=' Alkane combustion is complete in excess oxygen (CO₂, H₂O, heat) and incomplete with limited oxygen (toxic CO and soot). The source includes balanced examples and an alkane/alkene model activity.';
 alk.summary.ur+=' اضافی آکسیجن میں alkane کا مکمل احتراق CO₂، H₂O اور حرارت بناتا ہے؛ کم آکسیجن میں نامکمل احتراق زہریلا CO اور کالک بھی بناتا ہے۔ کتاب متوازن مساوات اور alkane/alkene ماڈل کی سرگرمی دیتی ہے۔';
 alk.summary.ps+=' په ډېرو اکسیجن کې د alkane بشپړ احتراق CO₂، H₂O او تودوخه جوړوي؛ په کمه اکسیجن کې نیمګړی احتراق زهرجن CO او لوګی هم جوړوي. کتاب متوازن معادلې او د alkane/alkene ماډل فعالیت لري.';
 ole.summary.en+=' Alkenes have at least one C=C bond and formula CₙH₂ₙ; the source lists and diagrams the first five homologues. IUPAC names use the longest chain containing the double bond, the lowest bond locant and −ene. Ethanol dehydration with concentrated H₂SO₄ at 180°C produces ethene and water.';
 ole.summary.ur+=' Alkenes میں کم از کم ایک C=C بند اور فارمولا CₙH₂ₙ ہوتا ہے؛ کتاب پہلے پانچ اراکین کی فہرست اور ساختیں دیتی ہے۔ IUPAC میں double bond والی طویل ترین زنجیر، کم ترین locant اور −ene استعمال ہوتا ہے۔ concentrated H₂SO₄ کے ساتھ 180°C پر ethanol کی dehydration سے ethene اور پانی بنتے ہیں۔';
 ole.summary.ps+=' Alkenes لږ تر لږه یو C=C بند او CₙH₂ₙ فورمول لري؛ کتاب د لومړیو پنځو غړو لړ او جوړښتونه ښيي. په IUPAC کې د double bond لرونکې تر ټولو اوږده ځنځیر، ټیټ locant او −ene کارېږي. له concentrated H₂SO₄ سره په 180°C کې د ethanol dehydration ethene او اوبه جوړوي.';
 const svg='<svg viewBox="0 0 560 150" role="img" aria-label="Coded alkene double-bond series"><g fill="#e0f2fe" stroke="#0369a1" stroke-width="2"><rect x="20" y="45" width="145" height="55" rx="8"/><rect x="205" y="45" width="145" height="55" rx="8"/><rect x="390" y="45" width="145" height="55" rx="8"/></g><g fill="#0f172a" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14"><text x="92" y="68">Ethene</text><text x="92" y="88">CH₂=CH₂</text><text x="277" y="68">Propene</text><text x="277" y="88">CH₂=CH−CH₃</text><text x="462" y="68">1-Butene</text><text x="462" y="88">CH₂=CH−CH₂−CH₃</text><text x="280" y="135">C=C position receives the lowest possible number</text></g></svg>';
