 add(t,7,'Hydrocarbons unit key points','The recap states hydrocarbons contain only C/H and are non-polar covalent; alkanes have only single bonds, formula CnH2n+2, while cycloalkanes have CnH2n; defines addition, hydrogenation, nascent hydrogen, reduction, substitution and combustion; distinguishes incomplete combustion; defines alkenes/olefins and elimination/dehydration/dehydrohalogenation; reviews halogen and hydrogen-halide addition, Baeyer unsaturation test, and alkynes with formula CnH2n−2.');
